// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/checkout_contact.t27 -- the contact details a checkout requires, and the
; shape a typed phone number has after normalization.
; This contract owns three things and nothing else: what a phone must look like once the
; normalizer has run, what a checkout blocker is and the closed set of them, and which fields
; a checkout may refuse to proceed without. It stops at the boundary of every neighbour: the
; fulfilment modes and the checkout join belong to turbobaby/commerce, whether a delivery
; destination is complete belongs to turbobaby/delivery-terms, the total belongs to
; turbobaby/order-money, the country calling code is a field of turbobaby/market, the blocker
; sentences are keys resolved under turbobaby/locale-policy, and how a refusal reaches the
; customer's screen belongs to turbobaby/client-errors.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). THE TWO CLIENT GATES DEMAND THE SAME SUBJECTS AND MEASURE THREE OF
; THEM AGAINST A DIFFERENT STRING: six subjects then, five since the 20+ box left on 2026-09-25
; (section (5)). The button gate takes six arguments and names five refusal reasons
; (src/trios/store.rs:451-458, enum at src/trios/store.rs:419-426), and in the name, phone and
; address rows it tests emptiness on the TRIMMED string and the length cap on the RAW one
; (src/trios/store.rs:467, :470, :473). The submit handler reaches the same subjects -- it refuses
; a missing identity at src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:893-897 (and, until 2026-09-25, an
; unticked age box at :898-902) before calling the validator at :904-910 -- but the validator
; caps the TRIMMED string in all three fields (src/trios/store.rs:505, :511, :522). So a value
; whose content fits the cap and whose surrounding whitespace does not is refused by the button
; and admitted by the handler: the customer gets a greyed-out button and a "too long" sentence
; for a field the validator would have passed. That is the same dead-button failure the gate
; was written to end (src/trios/store.rs:1049-1051).
;   The third gate is the server, and it requires the PRESENCE of ZERO of the four
; contact-bearing fields: customer_name is optional and only length-capped
; (src/api/orders.rs:117-121), customer_phone is optional and shape-checked only when present
; (src/api/orders.rs:122-134), delivery_address has no presence check, no cap and a bare TEXT
; column (migrations/044_order_delivery_fields.sql:5), and a missing telegram_id is not a
; refusal but a branch into an anonymous rate limit (src/api/orders.rs:884-899). Two of the five
; blockers have no server counterpart of any kind.
;   The repository does have an agreement test, and it is why the split has stayed invisible.
; src/trios/store.rs:1047-1068 asserts the button and the validator agree over FIVE hand-written
; rows (src/trios/store.rs:1054-1058), and not one carries a leading or trailing space. Five
; rows, zero of them padded: proven exactly where it cannot fail; one padded row turns it red.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED (every citation opened on 2026-09-21).
;   (1) The brief's claim -- that the checkout's default country calling code is hardcoded and
;       unwired to the market profile -- is FALSE as shipped. The code is not spelled here even
;       to be refuted, because this file promises below that it spells none.
;       src/trios/store.rs:325 defines DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE as
;       crate::trios::market::MARKET_DIALING.default_calling_code; src/trios/market.rs:92 holds
;       the value; data/fleet_seed.json:30 holds the deployment copy;
;       tests/market_clock_wiring.rs:256-258 fails if the Rust constant and the seed disagree;
;       scripts/verify_fleet_seed.py:171 pins the seed field's shape. The debt is real but
;       narrower, and it is pinned below instead: the profile is a compile-time &'static str
;       (src/trios/market.rs:86 and :92), so a market swap is a recompile -- src/trios/market.rs
;       says so in its own words at :69-71 -- and the profile reaches exactly ONE of the
;       normalizer's five branches (src/trios/store.rs:401). A second country's calling code is
;       emitted from a literal inside a format string at src/trios/store.rs:392, under no
;       profile at all. So "the default is unwired" is refuted and "one branch of five is
;       wired" is the measured fact.
;   (2) DECISIONS.md:351 still lists the checkout's calling-code default among the unwired debt
;       of issue #35. That sentence is now stale against src/trios/store.rs:325, and it is
;       the tripwire this file arms. Issue #35 has no body in this repository: DECISIONS.md:351
;       is the only place it is named AS AN ISSUE -- the same token occurs ten more times under
;       docs/reports/, where it is a wave number -- so no figure of the issue's is quoted here.
;   (3) Survey line corrections. normalize_phone is at src/trios/store.rs:366, not :356 -- :356
;       falls inside its doc comment, which opens at :355. The fulfilment mode is an ENUM, not
;       a struct, and spans src/trios/store.rs:333-354 including requires_address at :351-353.
;       The legacy CartItem constructors at src/trios/store.rs:23-95 are five, and the live
;       checkout screen calls FOUR of them (src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:295-309,
;       constructor calls at :300, :303, :305 and :306): new_tea_set at src/trios/store.rs:83
;       has zero call sites in src/ and tests/.
;   (4) A REFUTATION OF THIS FILE'S OWN FIRST DRAFT, kept because the next reader will make the
;       same mistake. validate_checkout_for really does lack a has_telegram_id parameter
;       (src/trios/store.rs:495-501; until 2026-09-25 the age box was a second one it lacked),
;       and it is tempting to call the handler short of the button. It is not. The function has
;       exactly one production call site, src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:904, and that call
;       site supplies the subject itself, immediately above, at :893-897 (the age box at :898-902
;       too, until it left). Every entry into the submit path goes through that closure
;       (src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:877, called at :1133, :1601 and :1680), so there is no
;       reachable order that the button refuses for a missing identity and the handler admits.
;       The function's argument list is a fact about the function; the gate is the call site. The
;       shipped agreement test passing `true` for identity at src/trios/store.rs:1061 is therefore
;       correct rather than a hole -- the hole is the padding the same five rows also lack.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES: D14 (DECISIONS.md:186-200) forbids a phone number in this
; repository in any form, and this contract is about phone numbers, so the refusal is
; load-bearing rather than decorative. Every rule below is written in digit COUNTS and named
; shape flags; no numeral sequence that could be dialled appears, not as an example, not as a
; fixture, not in a test. No address, no customer name, no Telegram handle. It states no
; calling code digits -- the market owns those. It computes no total, decides no delivery
; coverage, names no fulfilment discriminant of its own, and quotes no shipped Cyrillic string:
; the blocker sentences are cited by path only.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-checkout-contact;

pub const KIND : str = "contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/checkout-contact";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby checkout contact fields and phone normalization";
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";
pub const CORE_IMPLEMENTATION : str = "src/trios/store.rs";
pub const SCREEN_IMPLEMENTATION : str = "src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs";
; Addresses into that screen re-taken 2026-09-21 and re-read at their new lines, after the
; unreachable 409 arm was deleted and a cart-price refusal was added above the identity check:
; the closure :848 -> :877, the identity refusal :852-856 -> :893-897, the age box
; :857-861 -> :898-902, the validator call :863-869 -> :904-910, the three entries
; :1100/:1559/:1638 -> :1133/:1601/:1680, and the phone format :980 -> :1019. Every CLAIM in
; this file is unchanged; only the addresses moved. The new refusal is a SEVENTH subject the
; handler reaches before the six counted here -- an unpriced cart, owned by
; turbobaby/webapp-bridge -- and it refuses earlier than all six, so nothing this file says
; about the six is affected by it.
pub const SERVER_IMPLEMENTATION : str = "src/api/orders.rs";
pub const MESSAGE_IMPLEMENTATION : str = "src/trios/i18n.rs";

; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Reuse, not restatement. t27c has no imports; a neighbour is named by its ID string and a
; test pins the literal. Each of these owns a decision this file consumes as one argument.
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; turbobaby/market owns the country calling code as a profile field. This file never spells a
; calling code; it only counts how many normalizer branches read one.
pub const REUSES_MARKET_ID : str = "turbobaby/market";
; turbobaby/commerce owns the fulfilment discriminants and the checkout decision. This file
; takes "does this mode require an address" as a bare bool and names no mode.
pub const REUSES_COMMERCE_ID : str = "turbobaby/commerce";
; turbobaby/delivery-terms owns delivery_destination_ready. An address field being non-empty
; is a form fact; whether the destination leg is complete is that contract's answer, not this
; one's, and the two are deliberately not the same predicate.
pub const REUSES_DELIVERY_TERMS_ID : str = "turbobaby/delivery-terms";
; turbobaby/order-money owns the total. No amount appears below.
pub const REUSES_ORDER_MONEY_ID : str = "turbobaby/order-money";
; turbobaby/locale-policy owns the published locale set the blocker keys resolve in.
pub const REUSES_LOCALE_POLICY_ID : str = "turbobaby/locale-policy";
; turbobaby/client-errors owns how a refusal is rendered to the customer.
pub const REUSES_CLIENT_ERRORS_ID : str = "turbobaby/client-errors";
; turbobaby/request-identity owns whether a request carries a customer at all. This file takes
; that as the bare bool has_identity and decides nothing about how identity is established.
pub const REUSES_REQUEST_IDENTITY_ID : str = "turbobaby/request-identity";
pub const REUSED_CONTRACT_COUNT : u8 = 7;
; turbobaby/legacy-retirement is named further down as the owner of a QUESTION rather than of a
; decision this file consumes, so it is deliberately outside the count above.

; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; (1) WHAT A PHONE MUST LOOK LIKE AFTER NORMALIZATION
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Bounds measured at src/trios/store.rs:368 (trimmed input, non-empty and at most 50 chars)
; and src/trios/store.rs:375 (extracted ASCII digits, at least 5 and at most 15). Fifteen is
; the E.164 ceiling. Five is NOT an E.164 rule -- the standard sets no floor -- it is this
; repository's own guard, and it is recorded as such so nobody defends it as a standard.
pub const PHONE_DIGITS_MAX : u8 = 15;
pub const PHONE_DIGITS_MAX_IS_THE_E164_CEILING : bool = true;
pub const PHONE_DIGITS_MIN : u8 = 5;
pub const PHONE_DIGITS_MIN_IS_AN_E164_RULE : bool = false;
pub const PHONE_TRIMMED_CHARS_MAX : u8 = 50;

; Every accepting branch of src/trios/store.rs:366-407 returns a string beginning with '+'
; followed by digits only: :381, :386, :392 and :406 write the plus themselves, and :401 takes
; it from the market profile's own spelling of the code.
pub const NORMALIZED_PHONE_LEADS_WITH_PLUS : bool = true;
pub const NORMALIZED_PHONE_HOLDS_DIGITS_ONLY_AFTER_THE_PLUS : bool = true;

pub fn phone_digits_admitted(digits: u8) bool {
  return digits >= PHONE_DIGITS_MIN and digits <= PHONE_DIGITS_MAX;
}

pub fn phone_trimmed_length_admitted(trimmed_chars: u8) bool {
  return trimmed_chars >= 1 and trimmed_chars <= PHONE_TRIMMED_CHARS_MAX;
}

; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; (2) THE NORMALIZER'S BRANCHES, AND HOW MANY OF THEM THE MARKET REACHES
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Five accepting shapes, in the precedence src/trios/store.rs:380-406 tries them. They are
; named by the property of the input that selects them, never by a number: a leading plus
; (:380), two leading zeros (:384), an eleven-digit run behind a single foreign trunk digit
; (:391), a single leading zero (:399), and everything else that survived the bounds (:406).
; The caller supplies each property as a bool; this file derives no digit from any number and
; holds none.
pub const BRANCH_REFUSED : u8 = 0;
pub const BRANCH_LEADING_PLUS : u8 = 1;
pub const BRANCH_IDD_ZEROS : u8 = 2;
pub const BRANCH_FOREIGN_TRUNK : u8 = 3;
pub const BRANCH_NATIONAL_TRUNK_ZERO : u8 = 4;
pub const BRANCH_BARE_INTERNATIONAL : u8 = 5;
pub const BRANCH_COUNT : u8 = 5;
pub const BRANCH_NAMES : [5]str = [
  "leading_plus",
  "idd_zeros",
  "foreign_trunk",
  "national_trunk_zero",
  "bare_international"
];

; The IDD and national-trunk branches re-check the floor AFTER stripping their prefix and
; refuse rather than fall through (src/trios/store.rs:385-388 and :400-403). That second check
; is the only place where a number inside the outer bounds can still be rejected, and the
; subtractions below cannot underflow because phone_digits_admitted has already run.
pub fn normalizer_branch(trimmed_chars: u8, digits: u8, has_leading_plus: bool, has_two_leading_zeros: bool, is_foreign_trunk_shape: bool, has_one_leading_zero: bool) u8 {
  if (!phone_trimmed_length_admitted(trimmed_chars)) {
    return BRANCH_REFUSED;
  }
  if (!phone_digits_admitted(digits)) {
    return BRANCH_REFUSED;
  }
  if (has_leading_plus) {
    return BRANCH_LEADING_PLUS;
  }
  if (has_two_leading_zeros) {
    if (digits - 2 >= PHONE_DIGITS_MIN) {
      return BRANCH_IDD_ZEROS;
    }
    return BRANCH_REFUSED;
  }
  if (is_foreign_trunk_shape) {
    return BRANCH_FOREIGN_TRUNK;
  }
  if (has_one_leading_zero) {
    if (digits - 1 >= PHONE_DIGITS_MIN) {
      return BRANCH_NATIONAL_TRUNK_ZERO;
    }
    return BRANCH_REFUSED;
  }
  return BRANCH_BARE_INTERNATIONAL;
}

pub fn normalizer_refuses(branch: u8) bool {
  return branch == BRANCH_REFUSED;
}

pub fn branch_is_accepting(branch: u8) bool {
  return branch >= BRANCH_LEADING_PLUS and branch <= BRANCH_BARE_INTERNATIONAL;
}

; The tripwire the brief asked for, measured rather than assumed. src/trios/store.rs:401 is the
; single site that reads the market profile; src/trios/store.rs:392 emits another country's
; code from a literal. Swapping the deployment's market changes one branch in five.
pub fn branch_reads_the_market_profile(branch: u8) bool {
  return branch == BRANCH_NATIONAL_TRUNK_ZERO;
}

pub const BRANCHES_READING_THE_MARKET_PROFILE : u8 = 1;
pub const COUNTRY_CODE_LITERALS_INSIDE_THE_NORMALIZER : u8 = 1;

pub fn market_swap_reaches_every_branch() bool {
  return BRANCHES_READING_THE_MARKET_PROFILE == BRANCH_COUNT;
}

; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; (3) THE MARKET TRIPWIRE: THE CODE IS WIRED AND THE DECISION RECORD SAYS IT IS NOT
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-21. A tripwire that fires on a citation is worth exactly what the citation is
; worth, so every line this section stands on was re-opened rather than trusted, and each one still
; lands where it is said to:
;   DECISIONS.md:351 still carries the stale sentence, word for word -- "+66 default) is unwired
;     debt tracked in #35". It is also the ONLY occurrence of "#35" anywhere in DECISIONS.md, which
;     is what makes ISSUE_35_OCCURRENCES_AS_AN_ISSUE a 1 and not a survey of a common token; the
;     ten other hits are under docs/reports/ and are wave numbers, re-counted today at ten.
;   src/trios/store.rs:325 is still the wired const, reading
;     crate::trios::market::MARKET_DIALING.default_calling_code.
;   src/trios/market.rs:86 is still the profile field and :92 still holds the value; :69-71 still
;     says in the source's own words that a market swap is an edit here and in the seed.
;   data/fleet_seed.json:30 still holds the deployment copy, tests/market_clock_wiring.rs:256-258
;     still fails when the constant and the seed disagree, and scripts/verify_fleet_seed.py:171
;     still pins the field's shape.
;   src/trios/store.rs:401 is still the SINGLE read of DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE in the normalizer --
;     grep gives two hits in the whole file, the declaration at :325 and that one use -- and
;     src/trios/store.rs:392 still emits a second country's code from a literal under no profile.
;
; And the thing this section must never become: nowhere does this contract assert the stale claim
; as fact. The record's sentence is carried as a claim ABOUT THE RECORD
; (DECISION_RECORD_STILL_CALLS_IT_UNWIRED) and never as a claim about the code; the claim about the
; code is CALLING_CODE_IS_WIRED_TO_THE_PROFILE, and it is true. The two disagreeing is precisely
; what arms the tripwire, so collapsing them would disarm it while looking tidier.
pub const CALLING_CODE_IS_WIRED_TO_THE_PROFILE : bool = true;
pub const PROFILE_IS_A_COMPILE_TIME_CONSTANT : bool = true;
pub const SEED_AND_CONSTANT_ARE_PINNED_BY_A_TEST : bool = true;
pub const DECISION_RECORD_STILL_CALLS_IT_UNWIRED : bool = true;
pub const DECISION_RECORD_CITATION : str = "DECISIONS.md:351";
pub const DECISION_RECORD_CITATION_REVERIFIED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";
pub const DECISION_RECORD_CITATION_STILL_LANDS : bool = true;
pub const THIS_FILE_ASSERTS_THE_STALE_CLAIM_AS_FACT : bool = false;
pub const ISSUE_35_OCCURRENCES_IN_DECISIONS : u8 = 1;
pub const ISSUE_35_TOKEN_OCCURRENCES_UNDER_DOCS_REPORTS : u8 = 10;
pub const DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE_READ_SITES_IN_THE_NORMALIZER : u8 = 1;

; A tripwire whose citation no longer lands is not armed, it is merely loud. Both halves are
; required: the record must still say the stale thing AT the line cited, and the code must still be
; wired.
pub fn tripwire_citation_is_sound(citation_lands: bool, asserts_stale_claim_as_fact: bool) bool {
  return citation_lands and !asserts_stale_claim_as_fact;
}
pub const ISSUE_35_BODY_IS_PUBLISHED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const ISSUE_35_OCCURRENCES_AS_AN_ISSUE : u8 = 1;
pub const ISSUE_35_NOTE : str = "Issue #35 is named as an issue exactly once, at DECISIONS.md:351: no body, no tracker file, no figure. The token also appears ten times under docs/reports/, but there it is a WAVE number and not this issue, which is why the count above is scoped to the issue rather than to the string. This contract therefore cites the decision record's sentence and never the issue's contents, and it states no number whose only provenance would be a ticket nobody in this repository can open.";
pub const MARKET_GAP_NOTE : str = "What remains open is not the checkout default. It is that the profile is a compile-time constant rather than a value read from the verified seed at runtime, and that only the national-trunk branch consults it at all. A deployment moved to another market by editing the seed alone would keep normalizing with the compiled code, and the foreign-trunk branch would keep emitting a third country's code regardless.";

; Armed while the shipped code and the record that describes it disagree. Disarming it means
; correcting DECISIONS.md:351, not editing this file.
pub fn record_matches_the_code(code_is_wired: bool, record_says_unwired: bool) bool {
  return code_is_wired != record_says_unwired;
}

pub fn tripwire_is_armed(code_is_wired: bool, record_says_unwired: bool) bool {
  return !record_matches_the_code(code_is_wired, record_says_unwired);
}

; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; (4) THE OTHER CONTACT FIELDS, AND THE TRIM ASYMMETRY ALL THREE SHARE
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Caps at src/trios/store.rs:467 (name), :470 (phone) and :473 (address). In all three the
; content test reads the TRIMMED string -- directly for name and address, and through the
; normalizer's own trim at src/trios/store.rs:367-368 for the phone -- while the length cap
; reads the RAW one, so surrounding whitespace counts against the cap. The validator behind the
; same button caps the TRIMMED string instead (src/trios/store.rs:505, :511, :522). This is not
; a cosmetic difference and it is not merely a widened refusal: it is the ONE place where the
; two client gates disagree, and the direction is always the same -- the button refuses what
; the handler would admit, so the customer meets a dead button rather than a lost order.
pub const NAME_CHARS_MAX : u16 = 200;
pub const ADDRESS_CHARS_MAX : u16 = 500;
; The button adds a RAW cap of its own on the phone at src/trios/store.rs:470, on top of the
; TRIMMED cap the normalizer already applies at src/trios/store.rs:368. Same number, different
; string, which is exactly how the split hides.
pub const PHONE_RAW_CHARS_MAX_AT_THE_BUTTON : u16 = 50;
pub const EMPTINESS_IS_MEASURED_AFTER_TRIM : bool = true;
pub const LENGTH_CAP_IS_MEASURED_BEFORE_TRIM_AT_THE_BUTTON : bool = true;
pub const LENGTH_CAP_IS_MEASURED_AFTER_TRIM_AT_THE_HANDLER : bool = true;
pub const CAP_AND_EMPTINESS_READ_THE_SAME_STRING : bool = false;
pub const FIELDS_SHARING_THE_TRIM_ASYMMETRY : u8 = 3;
pub const FIELDS_SHARING_THE_TRIM_ASYMMETRY_NAMES : [3]str = ["name", "phone", "address"];

pub fn padding_can_refuse_an_inside_cap_field(content_chars: u16, padding_chars: u16, cap: u16) bool {
  return content_chars <= cap and content_chars + padding_chars > cap;
}

; One field, judged by the button (src/trios/store.rs:467, :470, :473) and by the validator
; (src/trios/store.rs:502-526). Same subject, same cap, different string measured.
pub fn button_field_ok(trimmed_chars: u16, raw_chars: u16, cap: u16) bool {
  return trimmed_chars >= 1 and raw_chars <= cap;
}

pub fn handler_field_ok(trimmed_chars: u16, cap: u16) bool {
  return trimmed_chars >= 1 and trimmed_chars <= cap;
}

pub fn padding_splits_the_two_gates(trimmed_chars: u16, raw_chars: u16, cap: u16) bool {
  return !button_field_ok(trimmed_chars, raw_chars, cap) and handler_field_ok(trimmed_chars, cap);
}

pub fn name_admitted(trimmed_chars: u16, raw_chars: u16) bool {
  return trimmed_chars >= 1 and raw_chars <= NAME_CHARS_MAX;
}

; An address is needed ONLY for delivery, and whether this mode is a delivery is
; turbobaby/commerce's discriminant reaching us as one bool. The cap, however, sits OUTSIDE the
; mode test at src/trios/store.rs:473: an over-long address blocks a pickup too, where no
; address was wanted in the first place. Reproduced deliberately.
pub fn address_admitted(mode_requires_address: bool, trimmed_chars: u16, raw_chars: u16) bool {
  if (mode_requires_address and trimmed_chars == 0) {
    return false;
  }
  return raw_chars <= ADDRESS_CHARS_MAX;
}

; What this file will NOT claim. A non-empty address string is a filled form field and nothing
; more; whether a destination can actually be reached is turbobaby/delivery-terms' answer
; through its delivery_destination_ready producer, and the two predicates are not equal.
pub fn a_filled_address_means_the_destination_is_ready() bool {
  return false;
}

; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; (5) WHAT A BLOCKER IS, AND THE FULL SET
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Five reasons, closed (src/trios/store.rs:419-426), pushed in form order so the list reads
; top-to-bottom like the screen (src/trios/store.rs:460-479). BLOCKER_CLEAR is this contract's
; own sentinel for an empty list; the shipped code returns an empty Vec and names no such
; value, so it is deliberately placed outside the enum's range. There were six until
; 2026-09-25: the sixth, the age box, is recorded below with the owner's answer that removed it,
; and the enum line and the push that held it are comments now (src/trios/store.rs:425 and
; :476-478), so no line the paragraphs of this file cite has moved. Gate 3 binds BLOCKER_COUNT
; to the number of reasons checkout_blockers pushes, so a sixth push turns it red.
pub const BLOCKER_NO_TELEGRAM : u8 = 0;
pub const BLOCKER_EMPTY_CART : u8 = 1;
pub const BLOCKER_NAME : u8 = 2;
pub const BLOCKER_PHONE : u8 = 3;
pub const BLOCKER_ADDRESS : u8 = 4;
pub const BLOCKER_COUNT : u8 = 5;
pub const BLOCKER_CLEAR : u8 = 255;
pub const BLOCKER_NAMES : [5]str = [
  "no_telegram",
  "empty_cart",
  "name",
  "phone",
  "address"
];

pub fn blocker_is_known(blocker: u8) bool {
  return blocker < BLOCKER_COUNT;
}

; Each blocker carries a translation key (src/trios/store.rs:430-447) whose sentences ship at
; src/trios/i18n.rs:872-887 and :1472-1487. Cited by path and never quoted: two of them embed
; an example number (src/trios/i18n.rs:876 and :1476), which D14 keeps out of this file.
; Coverage is proven, not assumed: src/trios/store.rs:1070-1090 walks all five blockers against
; both published locales and fails on an empty or untranslated sentence. Which locales are
; published is turbobaby/locale-policy's answer, and the count is not restated here.
pub const EVERY_BLOCKER_CARRIES_A_MESSAGE_KEY : bool = true;
pub const BLOCKER_KEY_COVERAGE_IS_PROVEN_PER_PUBLISHED_LOCALE : bool = true;
pub const BLOCKER_SENTENCES_QUOTED_HERE : [0]str = [];

; The age blocker was inherited, not designed for this product: its shipped sentence was the
; cannabis age confirmation the bot forked with (src/trios/i18n.rs:881 and :1481, each a comment
; line since 2026-09-25), and D19 (DECISIONS.md:354) hid that heritage behind visibility flags
; without settling this gate -- its own closing paragraph lists what it does not settle. Whether
; a bike-rental checkout should keep the gate was turbobaby/legacy-retirement's question, and
; until 2026-09-25 this file recorded only that the gate was a member of the required set and
; one of the two reasons the server also enforced.
pub const AGE_BLOCKER_IS_INHERITED_HERITAGE : bool = true;
pub const AGE_BLOCKER_RETIREMENT_OWNER : str = "turbobaby/legacy-retirement";

; REMOVED 2026-09-25, FOR NOW -- the owner's decision. The owner answered that question on
; 2026-09-25, in answer 1 of a second numbered list put to him that day (numbered 1 to 5, the
; numbering confirmed by the owner): for now, we remove it. The Russian original is in
; DECISIONS.md, the D19 addendum of that date. The answer says "for now", so the removal is
; recorded as provisional: a later answer may bring the box back, and git history holds it all.
;   What left. Each line that held it is a comment of the same count now, so no line cited
; anywhere in the corpus moved: the enum variant and its push (src/trios/store.rs:425 and
; :476-478), the button's seventh argument (:458), the handler's refusal
; (src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:898-902), the box and its notice (:1334-1351), the trust
; block's age line (:1579), the request body's field (:1030), the server's refusal
; (src/api/orders.rs:145-148), and five i18n keys (AGE_GATE_I18N_KEYS_DELETED_NAMES). Four of
; the five were rendered: the box's label, the notice under it (which the handler also showed as
; its refusal), the trust line and the blocker sentence. The fifth, the sentence for a body code
; "age_not_confirmed", was never reachable: the server's refusal was a bare 422 with no body, and
; before the change the literal occurred only in the client's mapper (src/trios/checkout_errors.rs)
; and inside the key's own name -- no server path wrote it. No sentence was written in their place.
;   What stayed. POST /api/orders still ACCEPTS the field, because a bundle cached before the
; change still sends it true: serde reads it, validation no longer looks at it, and the orders
; column (migration 057, NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE) stores it as sent, absent as false. No migration
; was added, no row was written or deleted, and a stored order keeps what it recorded. The
; customer's saved checkout draft is not reached into: a draft that carries the field still
; restores (serde drops it), and the storage key an older build wrote the last answer under is
; neither read nor cleared. tests/integration_create_order.rs holds the endpoint to it: absent,
; false and true all meet the empty cart's 400, where absent and false met a 422 before.
pub const AGE_BLOCKER_REMOVED_AT : str = "2026-09-25";
pub const AGE_BLOCKER_REMOVED_BY_OWNER_ANSWER : u8 = 1;
pub const AGE_BLOCKER_REMOVAL_IS_PROVISIONAL : bool = true;
pub const AGE_BLOCKER_IS_IN_THE_REQUIRED_SET : bool = false;
pub const AGE_BLOCKER_WAS_IN_THE_REQUIRED_SET_BEFORE_2026_09_25 : bool = true;
; The retired code keeps its number. 5 is where the age blocker stood, and it now equals
; BLOCKER_COUNT, so blocker_is_known refuses it with no special case.
pub const BLOCKER_AGE_RETIRED : u8 = 5;
pub const BLOCKER_COUNT_BEFORE_2026_09_25 : u8 = 6;
pub const BLOCKER_NAMES_BEFORE_2026_09_25 : [6]str = [
  "no_telegram",
  "empty_cart",
  "name",
  "phone",
  "address",
  "age"
];
